ate: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error_rate 0.002 (was 0.18). No deployment of a never-healthy version was performed. Follow-ups: investigate root cause of v2.3.1 health-check failures and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt; confirm v2.3.1 remains blocked from redeploy until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2026-incident-1"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I can't tell whether it was created. I'll check the incident list before retrying so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01URLHHQQa51rdtFockvF2QG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.18 \u2192 0.002). The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, so I did not deploy anything that lacked a healthy production record and no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found INC-0001 already recorded with the full summary, so I did not create a duplicate page.\n\nFollow-ups for the on-call team: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures, and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt. v2.3.1 should stay blocked from redeploy until it is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}